# The reachable findings the vulncheck band accepts, one line per module and advisory.
#
#   module ~ advisory ~ reason
#
# Read by .dev/validate/vulncheck.sh. This is not a suppression list: every line is a claim the run has
# to satisfy. A reachable finding with no line here fails the check, and a line whose finding no longer
# occurs fails it just as loudly — the advisory it excuses is gone, so the line has to go. Wildcards are
# refused. The reason is mandatory: a line whose reason is empty is a line nobody can review.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# the standard library of the toolchain that builds
#
# Every row below is one class: an advisory against the standard library of go1.25.12, the toolchain the
# dev image currently carries, each fixed in go1.25.13. No go.mod names the standard library, so no pin
# in this tree can move these; they die wholesale when the image is rebuilt on a newer golang base, and
# this band then fails on every row until the rows are deleted — run vulncheck.sh --report and reseed.
#
. ~ GO-2026-5026 ~ standard library of the go1.25.12 toolchain in the dev image; fixed in go1.25.13 — dies at the next image rebuild
